{"id":"7447bbbe-d1dc-4c00-bbb0-8021e8904f75","object":"chat.completion","created":1791535933,"model":"deepseek-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"Recovered two full originals from offloaded keys (`call_00_P2W3Et1WKP56CCZ5DYIw4260_0` = acceptance record `5582561d…8627`; `call_00_XLbUErHdJlZOtOTR0sKn3636_0` = evaluation `6314170d…6892`). Values match the saved history exactly, so no re-read is required. Submitting the formal decision now.","reasoning_content":"Recovered full originals. Values confirmed:\n\nEvaluation 6314170d: candidate_id fixed-radius, comparison_identity 3c24b89e..., constraints task_bound limit 0.01 observed 0.0031314437885609334 satisfied true units m, evaluator evaluate.reach 1.0.0, metrics position_error m 0.0031314437885609334, original_execution_id 197bceb6..., source e2c5a5ed..., source_execution_id 197bceb6..., task_success true, validity valid, reason null.\n\nAcceptance 5582561d: accepted false, components (holding_speed limit 0.02 passed false value 0.026817670846968282; holding_position 0.0033622899352609014 passed true; evaluator:task_bound 0.01, 0.0031314437885609334 passed true; holding_coverage limit 6 passed true; force_bounds 1e-08 N 0.0 pass; solver_errors 0 count pass; execution_complete true; evaluation_validity valid; task_evaluator true), metrics, status valid_failure, protocol_id offline_reach_hold_v1, execution_id 197bceb6..., task_identity d0f438cf..., official_recorded_task_success true, new_backend_solves 0, continuous_time_guarantee false, timing deadline_misses 35 etc.\n\nNow verify the report fact once more (already have). Now submit.\n\nSchema: decision {investigation_id, report, disposition, adopted_claims, evidence_used, remaining_unknowns, reason}. Each adopted claim: {statement, supporting_facts, scope, support_explanation}. Each fact: {statement, reference, pointer, value, source_identity:{}}.\n\ninvestigation_id: \"fixed-C-offline-report\" (directory target).\nreport: directory report reference → {\"artifact_id\": \"66ff0f1c550ccd2117f33d64831ac206629a3858b01e50fb97fefc5106153abf\", \"media_type\": \"application/json\"}.\n\ndisposition: accept.\n\nadopted_claims: one claim supported by report fact.\n\nstatement: \"The saved official reach evaluation for the fixed-C (fixed-radius) execution reports a terminal tip position error of 0.0031314437885609334 m, within the 0.01 m task bound, with validity 'valid' and task_success true.\"\n\nHmm — but \"adopt only report-supported claims\" and the supporting_facts must be from report facts. The report fact statement is \"Saved official reach error\" with value 0.0031314437885609334 pointer /metrics/0/value. So the claim statement should be limited to what the report fact supports: the saved official reach error is 0.0031314437885609334 m. Wording about bound/validity/success comes from the evaluation source, which I put in evidence_used. To be safe, keep the claim statement narrowly about the reach error value, and mention within support_explanation that the value is drawn from the report fact with pointer /metrics/0/value at 6314170d, corroborated by evidence_used.\n\nActually I'll keep claim narrow: \"The saved official reach error recorded for the fixed-C evaluation is 0.0031314437885609334 m (position_error, in metres).\"\n\nsupporting_facts: [{statement: \"Saved official reach error\", reference: {artifact_id: \"6314170dd823eab26d13296eb5afee1cfe24cb2f5117334414d1d66e8d266892\", media_type: \"application/json\"}, pointer: \"/metrics/0/value\", value: 0.0031314437885609334, source_identity: {}}]\n\nscope: {\"candidate_id\": \"fixed-radius\", \"comparison_identity\": \"3c24b89e5c9abc7589dc69839f25d5050be1b212d31a2dec86dba230198c92c8\", \"evaluator\": \"evaluate.reach\", \"evaluator_version\": \"1.0.0\", \"original_execution_id\": \"197bceb6ff8f44b48a35bc4f79b3528d\", \"source_execution_id\": \"197bceb6ff8f44b48a35bc4f79b3528d\", \"validity\": \"valid\"}\n\nHmm, scope \"contains inspected source