accepted\" value false; \"/detail/status\" \"valid_failure\"; \"/detail/official_recorded_task_success\" true.\n7. identities: task identity, robot identity, execution id, seed, protocol_id.\n\nI'll include a reasonable set.\n\nremaining_unknowns: [\"Physical cause of the holding-speed exceedance is unassessed.\", \"Live-model compatibility and physical robot behaviour are unassessed (ideal tensions; omitted shear, stretch, torsion, tendon friction and actuator dynamics).\", \"Continuous-time holding behaviour is not guaranteed; the holding window is sampled (continuous_time_guarantee false, 6 inclusive uniform samples).\", \"Results cover only candidate 'fixed-radius' at seed 17, execution 197bceb6…, target [0.29, 0.035, 0.19]; other candidates/seeds/targets unassessed.\", \"Nested artifacts (simulation e2c5a5ed…, motion 27c1929f…, configuration 77a14067…, one_step_prediction_evidence 1e7ac586…) were not independently readable.\"]\n\nreason: full assessment + explanation of arrival/holding position/holding speed/joint outcome.\n\nLet me write the reason carefully, linked to evidence_used.\n\ndisposition: accept. But should the disposition reflect that the joint acceptance failed? The instruction: \"explain arrival, holding position, holding speed and joint outcome.\" And \"Acceptance of source-supported claims does not mean success of the robot task.\" So accept = accept the evidence/claims. I'll go with accept, and make reason explicit that joint acceptance is false.\n\nHmm, let me reconsider once more whether disposition should be \"accept\". Given the review's purpose is to decide the principal's judgment of the saved evidence: it's valid, complete, self-consistent, and honestly recorded as a failure. Accepting the evidence record is right; rejecting would imply fabrication, deferring would imply insufficient info. I'm comfortable with accept.\n\nNow submit with revision 1. Then get_receipt.\n\nLet me construct JSON.\n\nNote: value in facts can be number or object. I'll use exact numbers.\n\nLet me write it.","tool_calls":[{"index":0,"id":"call_00_4iI39KTtggRfG7ecZjCJ1957","type":"function","function":{"name":"submit_result","arguments":"{\"revision\": 1, \"decision\": {\"investigation_id\": \"fixed-C-offline-report\", \"report\": {\"artifact_id\": \"66ff0f1c550ccd2117f33d64831ac206629a3858b01e50fb97fefc5106153abf\", \"media_type\": \"application/json\"}, \"disposition\": \"accept\", \"adopted_claims\": [{\"statement\": \"The saved official reach error recorded for the fixed-C (candidate 'fixed-radius') execution is 0.0031314437885609334 m (position_error, in metres).\", \"supporting_facts\": [{\"statement\": \"Saved official reach error\", \"reference\": {\"artifact_id\": \"6314170dd823eab26d13296eb5afee1cfe24cb2f5117334414d1d66e8d266892\", \"media_type\": \"application/json\"}, \"pointer\": \"/metrics/0/value\", \"value\": 0.0031314437885609334, \"source_identity\": {}}], \"scope\": {\"candidate_id\": \"fixed-radius\", \"comparison_identity\": \"3c24b89e5c9abc7589dc69839f25d5050be1b212d31a2dec86dba230198c92c8\", \"evaluator\": \"evaluate.reach\", \"evaluator_version\": \"1.0.0\", \"original_execution_id\": \"197bceb6ff8f44b48a35bc4f79b3528d\", \"source_execution_id\": \"197bceb6ff8f44b48a35bc4f79b3528d\", \"source_artifact_id\": \"6314170dd823eab26d13296eb5afee1cfe24cb2f5117334414d1d66e8d266892\", \"validity\": \"valid\"}, \"support_explanation\": \"The extraction-only report records exactly one fact: statement 'Saved official reach error', value 0.0031314437885609334, at pointer /metrics/0/value of source 6314170d…6892. The directly read original of that source confirms metrics[0] = {name: position_error, units: m, value: 0.0031314437885609334}. The adopted claim is deliberately restricted to this recorded reach-error value; it asserts neither joint acceptance nor robot-task success.\"}], \"evidence_used\": [{\"statement\": \"Saved evaluation constraint task_bound: limit 0.01 m, observed 0.0031314437885609334 m, satisfied true\", \"reference\": {\"artifact_id\": \"6314170dd823eab26d13296eb5afee1cfe24cb2f5117334414d1d66e8d266892\", \"media_type\": \"application/json\"}, \"pointer\": \"/constraints/0\", \"value\": {\"name\": \"task_bound\", \"limit\": 0.01, \"observed\": 0.0031314437885609334, \"satisfied\": true, \"units\": \"m\"}, \"source_identity\": {}}, {\"statement\": \"Saved evaluation recorded validity 'valid' with reason null and task_success true\", \"reference\": {\"artifact_id\": \"6314170dd823eab26d13296eb5afee1cfe24cb2f5117334414d1d66e8d266892\", \"media_type\": \"application/json\"}, \"pointer\": \"/validity\", \"value\": \"valid\", \"source_identity\": {}}, {\"statement\": \"Saved evaluation recorded task_success true (historical evaluator evaluate.reach, arrival-only)\", \"reference\": {\"artifact_id\": \"6314170dd823eab26d13296eb5afee1cfe24cb2f5117334414d1d66e8d266892\", \"media_type\": \"application/json\"}, \"pointer\": \"/task_success\", \"value\": true, \"source_identity\": {}}, {\"statement\": \"Holding-window report: sampled settling available with continuous_time_guarantee false, position_limit_m 0.01, speed_limit_m_s 0.02, window_s 0.05, and passed false\", \"reference\": {\"artifact_id\": \"400226bfd9f0d75d698037f494987054f3030fce7813612c11f6f4d4e5d6ab13\", \"media_type\": \"application/json\"}, \"pointer\": \"/detail/sampled_settling\", \"value\": {\"available\": true, \"continuous_time_guarantee\": false, \"max_error_m\": 0.0033622899352609014, \"max_speed_m_s\": 0.026817670846968282, \"passed\": false, \"position_limit_m\": 0.01, \"speed_limit_m_s\": 0.02, \"window_s\": 0.05}, \"source_identity\": {}}, {\"statement\": \"Holding-window report: maximum sampled holding-window tip speed 0.026817670846968282 m/s exceeds the 0.02 m/s speed limit\", \"reference\": {\"artifact_id\": \"400226bfd9f0d75d698037f494987054f3030fce7813612c11f6f4d4e5d6ab13\", \"media_type\": \"application/json\"}, \"pointer\": \"/detail/sampled_settling/max_speed_m_s\", \"value\": 0.02